    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A per-model hint. Sparse: list only the models you have an opinion about; anything absent takes every field&apos;s default.</para>
<para><computeroutput>placement</computeroutput> is a hint, never a command: a host that cannot honour it downgrades and reports what it did — read <computeroutput>LoadModelResponse</computeroutput> rather than assuming.</para>
<para><computeroutput>hotwords</computeroutput> is <emphasis>not</emphasis> downgradable. Hotword biasing needs beam-search decoding, which a recognizer fixes when it is constructed, so it selects which recognizer this session is served. <computeroutput>HotwordBias_On</computeroutput> costs a few percent of decode time and changes that model&apos;s transcripts whether or not a lexicon is supplied; <computeroutput>HotwordBias_Off</computeroutput> makes <computeroutput>CreateVoiceInput</computeroutput> reject a <computeroutput>hotwordsStoragePath</computeroutput> with <computeroutput>HotwordBiasDisabled</computeroutput> (4106) instead of accepting it and biasing nothing. Left at <computeroutput>HotwordBias_Default</computeroutput>, the model&apos;s catalog entry decides. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
